reen saver emulation.","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"Connect USB Keyboard","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":2},{"title":"Enable WiiConnect24 via WiiLink","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":3},{"title":"Emulate Skylander Portal","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":4},{"title":"Aspect Ratio","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":5},{"title":"System Language","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":6},{"title":"Sound","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Misc Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":0,"row":7},{"title":"Insert SD Card","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › SD Card Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":1,"row":0},{"title":"Allow Writes to SD Card","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › SD Card Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":1,"row":1},{"title":"Automatically Sync with Folder","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › SD Card Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":1,"row":2},{"title":"Convert Folder to File Now","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › SD Card Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":1,"row":3},{"title":"Convert File to Folder Now","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › SD Card Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":1,"row":4},{"title":"Sensor Bar Position","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Wii Remote Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":2,"row":0},{"title":"IR Sensitivity","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Wii Remote Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":2,"row":1},{"title":"Speaker Volume","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Wii Remote Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":2,"row":2},{"title":"Enable Rumble","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Wii › Wii Remote Settings","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigWii","section":2,"row":3},{"title":"CPU Emulation Engine","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › CPU Options","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":0,"row":0},{"title":"Enable MMU","description":"Enables memory management unit emulation for game compatibility.","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › CPU Options","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"Pause on Panic","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › CPU Options","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":0,"row":2},{"title":"Enable Write-Back Cache (slow)","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › CPU Options","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":0,"row":3},{"title":"Enable Emulated CPU Clock Override","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › Clock Override","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":1,"row":0},{"title":"Enable VBI Frequency Override","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › VBI Frequency Override","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":2,"row":0},{"title":"Enable Emulated Memory Size Override","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › Memory Override","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":3,"row":0},{"title":"MEM1","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › Memory Override","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":3,"row":1},{"title":"MEM2","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › Memory Override","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":3,"row":2},{"title":"Enable Custom RTC","description":"","path":"Settings › Config › Advanced › Custom RTC Options","storyboard":"ConfigSettings","identifier":"SearchConfigAdvanced","section":4,"row":0},{"title":"Backend","description":"Selects which graphics API to use internally. The software renderer is extremely slow and only useful for debugging, so any of the other backends are recommended. Different games and different GPUs will behave differently on each backend, so for the best emulation experience it is recommended to try each and select the backend that is least problematic. If unsure, select OpenGL.","path":"Settings › Graphics › General › Basic","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsGeneral","section":0,"row":0},{"title":"Aspect Ratio","description":"Selects which aspect ratio to use when rendering. Auto: Uses the native aspect ratio Force 16:9: Mimics an analog TV with a widescreen aspect ratio. Force 4:3: Mimics a standard 4:3 analog TV. Stretch to Window: Stretches the picture to the window size. If unsure, select Auto.","path":"Settings › Graphics › General › Basic","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsGeneral","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"V-Sync","description":"Waits for vertical blanks in order to prevent tearing. Decreases performance if emulation speed is below 100%. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › General › Basic","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsGeneral","section":0,"row":2},{"title":"Shader Compilation Type","description":"","path":"Settings › Graphics › General › Shader Compilation","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsGeneral","section":1,"row":0},{"title":"Compile Shaders Before Starting","description":"Waits for all shaders to finish compiling before starting a game. Enabling this option may reduce stuttering or hitching for a short time after the game is started, at the cost of a longer delay before the game starts. For systems with two or fewer cores, it is recommended to enable this option, as a large shader queue may reduce frame rates. Otherwise, if unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › General › Shader Compilation","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsGeneral","section":1,"row":1},{"title":"Internal Resolution","description":"Controls the rendering resolution. A high resolution greatly improves visual quality, but also greatly increases GPU load and can cause issues in certain games. Generally speaking, the lower the internal resolution, the better performance will be. If unsure, select Native.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":0},{"title":"Texture Filtering","description":"Adjust the texture filtering. Anisotropic filtering enhances the visual quality of textures that are at oblique viewing angles. Force Nearest and Force Linear override the texture scaling filter selected by the game. Any option except 'Default' will alter the look of the game's textures and might cause issues in a small number of games. If unsure, select 'Default'.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"Scaled EFB Copy","description":"Greatly increases the quality of textures generated using render-to-texture effects. Slightly increases GPU load and causes relatively few graphical issues. Raising the internal resolution will improve the effect of this setting. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":2},{"title":"Disable Fog","description":"Makes distant objects more visible by removing fog, thus increasing the overall detail. Disabling fog will break some games which rely on proper fog emulation. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":3},{"title":"Disable Copy Filter","description":"Disables the blending of adjacent rows when copying the EFB. This is known in some games as \"deflickering\" or \"smoothing\". Disabling the filter has no effect on performance, but may result in a sharper image. Causes few graphical issues. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":4},{"title":"Per-Pixel Lighting","description":"Calculates lighting of 3D objects per-pixel rather than per-vertex, smoothing out the appearance of lit polygons and making individual triangles less noticeable. Rarely causes slowdowns or graphical issues. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":5},{"title":"Widescreen Hack","description":"Forces the game to output graphics for any aspect ratio. Use with \"Aspect Ratio\" set to \"Force 16:9\" to force 4:3-only games to run at 16:9. Rarely produces good results and often partially breaks graphics and game UIs. Unnecessary (and detrimental) if using any AR/Gecko-code widescreen patches. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":6},{"title":"Force 24-Bit Color","description":"Forces the game to render the RGB color channels in 24-bit, thereby increasing quality by reducing color banding. Has no impact on performance and causes few graphical issues. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":7},{"title":"Arbitrary Mipmap Detection","description":"Enables detection of arbitrary mipmaps, which some games use for special distance-based effects. May have false positives that result in blurry textures at increased internal resolution, such as in games that use very low resolution mipmaps. Disabling this can also reduce stutter in games that frequently load new textures. This feature is not compatible with GPU Texture Decoding. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Enhancements › Enhancements","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsEnhancements","section":0,"row":8},{"title":"Skip EFB Access from CPU","description":"Ignores any requests from the CPU to read from or write to the EFB. Improves performance in some games, but will disable all EFB-based graphical effects or gameplay-related features. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Embedded Frame Buffer (EFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":0,"row":0},{"title":"Store EFB Copies to Texture Only","description":"Stores EFB copies exclusively on the GPU, bypassing system memory. Causes graphical defects in a small number of games. Enabled = EFB Copies to Texture Disabled = EFB Copies to RAM (and Texture) If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Embedded Frame Buffer (EFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"Ignore Format Changes","description":"Ignores any changes to the EFB format. Improves performance in many games without any negative effect. Causes graphical defects in a small number of other games. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Embedded Frame Buffer (EFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":0,"row":2},{"title":"Defer EFB Copies to RAM","description":"Waits until the game synchronizes with the emulated GPU before writing the contents of EFB copies to RAM. Reduces the overhead of EFB RAM copies, providing a performance boost in many games, at the risk of breaking those which do not safely synchronize with the emulated GPU. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Embedded Frame Buffer (EFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":0,"row":3},{"title":"Accuracy","description":"","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Texture Cache","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":1,"row":0},{"title":"GPU Texture Decoding","description":"Enables texture decoding using the GPU instead of the CPU. This may result in performance gains in some scenarios, or on systems where the CPU is the bottleneck. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Texture Cache","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":1,"row":1},{"title":"Store XFB Copies to Texture Only","description":"Stores XFB copies exclusively on the GPU, bypassing system memory. Causes graphical defects in a small number of games. Enabled = XFB Copies to Texture Disabled = XFB Copies to RAM (and Texture) If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › External Frame Buffer (XFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":2,"row":0},{"title":"Immediately Present XFB","description":"Displays XFB copies as soon as they are created, instead of waiting for scanout. Can cause graphical defects in some games if the game doesn't expect all XFB copies to be displayed. However, turning this setting on reduces latency. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › External Frame Buffer (XFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":2,"row":1},{"title":"Skip Presenting Duplicate Frames","description":"Skips presentation of duplicate frames (XFB copies) in 25fps/30fps games. This may improve performance on low-end devices, while making frame pacing less consistent. Disable this option as well as enabling V-Sync for optimal frame pacing. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › External Frame Buffer (XFB)","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":2,"row":2},{"title":"Fast Depth Calculation","description":"Uses a less accurate algorithm to calculate depth values. Causes issues in a few games, but can result in a decent speed increase depending on the game and/or GPU. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Other","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":3,"row":0},{"title":"Vertex Rounding","description":"Rounds 2D vertices to whole pixels and rounds the viewport size to a whole number. Fixes graphical problems in some games at higher internal resolutions. This setting has no effect when native internal resolution is used. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Other","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":3,"row":1},{"title":"Disable Bounding Box","description":"Disables bounding box emulation. This may improve GPU performance significantly, but some games will break. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Other","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":3,"row":2},{"title":"Save Texture Cache to State","description":"Includes the contents of the embedded frame buffer (EFB) and upscaled EFB copies in save states. Fixes missing and/or non-upscaled textures/objects when loading states at the cost of additional save/load time. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Other","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":3,"row":3},{"title":"VBI Skip","description":"Skips Vertical Blank Interrupts when lag is detected, allowing for smooth audio playback when emulation speed is not 100%. WARNING: Can cause freezes and compatibility issues. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Hacks › Other","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsHacks","section":3,"row":4},{"title":"Show FPS","description":"Shows the number of distinct frames rendered per second as a measure of visual smoothness. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":0},{"title":"Show VPS","description":"Shows the number of frames rendered per second as a measure of emulation speed. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"Show % Speed","description":"Shows the % speed of emulation compared to full speed. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":2},{"title":"Show Frame Times","description":"Shows the average time in ms between each distinct rendered frame alongside the standard deviation. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":3},{"title":"Show VBlank Times","description":"Shows the average time in ms between each rendered frame alongside the standard deviation. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":4},{"title":"Show Performance Graphs","description":"Shows frametime graph along with statistics as a representation of emulation performance. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":5},{"title":"Log Render Time to File","description":"Logs the render time of every frame to User/Logs/render_time.txt. Use this feature to measure Dolphin's performance. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":6},{"title":"Show Speed Colors","description":"Changes the color of the FPS counter depending on emulation speed. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Performance Statistics","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":0,"row":7},{"title":"Show Statistics","description":"Shows various rendering statistics. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Debugging","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":1,"row":0},{"title":"Enable API Validation Layers","description":"Enables validation of API calls made by the video backend, which may assist in debugging graphical issues. On the Vulkan and D3D backends, this also enables debug symbols for the compiled shaders. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Debugging","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":1,"row":1},{"title":"Load Custom Textures","description":"Loads custom textures from User/Load/Textures/<game_id>/ and User/Load/DynamicInputTextures/<game_id>/. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Utility","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":2,"row":0},{"title":"Prefetch Custom Textures","description":"Caches custom textures to system RAM on startup. This can require exponentially more RAM but fixes possible stuttering. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Utility","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":2,"row":1},{"title":"Disable EFB VRAM Copies","description":"Disables the VRAM copy of the EFB, forcing a round-trip to RAM. Inhibits all upscaling. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Utility","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":2,"row":2},{"title":"Enable Graphics Mods","description":"Loads graphics mods from User/Load/GraphicsMods/. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Utility","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":2,"row":3},{"title":"Crop","description":"Crops the picture from its native aspect ratio to 4:3 or 16:9. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Misc","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":3,"row":0},{"title":"Enable Progressive Scan","description":"Enables progressive scan if supported by the emulated software. Most games don't have any issue with this. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Misc","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":3,"row":1},{"title":"Backend Multithreading","description":"Enables multithreaded command submission in backends where supported. Enabling this option may result in a performance improvement on systems with more than two CPU cores. Currently, this is limited to the Vulkan backend. If unsure, leave this checked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Misc","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":3,"row":2},{"title":"Prefer VS for Point/Line Expansion","description":"","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Misc","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":3,"row":3},{"title":"Cull Vertices on the CPU","description":"Cull vertices on the CPU to reduce the number of draw calls required. May affect performance and draw statistics. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Misc","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":3,"row":4},{"title":"Defer EFB Cache Invalidation","description":"Defers invalidation of the EFB access cache until a GPU synchronization command is executed. If disabled, the cache will be invalidated with every draw call. May improve performance in some games which rely on CPU EFB Access at the cost of stability. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Experimental","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":4,"row":0},{"title":"Manual Texture Sampling","description":"Use a manual implementation of texture sampling instead of the graphics backend's built-in functionality. This setting can fix graphical issues in some games on certain GPUs, most commonly vertical lines on FMVs. In addition to this, enabling Manual Texture Sampling will allow for correct emulation of texture wrapping special cases (at 1x IR or when scaled EFB is disabled, and with custom textures disabled) and better emulates Level of Detail calculation. This comes at the cost of potentially worse performance, especially at higher internal resolutions; additionally, Anisotropic Filtering is currently incompatible with Manual Texture Sampling. If unsure, leave this unchecked.","path":"Settings › Graphics › Advanced › Experimental","storyboard":"GraphicsSettings","identifier":"SearchGraphicsAdvanced","section":4,"row":1},{"title":"Fastmem","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › General","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":0,"row":0},{"title":"Sync on Idle Skip","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › General","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":0,"row":1},{"title":"Attach Virtual MFi Controller","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › Controllers","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":1,"row":0},{"title":"Reset Launch Times","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › Utility","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":2,"row":0},{"title":"Force Start Motion Updates","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › Utility","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":2,"row":1},{"title":"User Folder","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › Environment","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":3,"row":0},{"title":"JIT Acquisition","description":"Shows the status of just-in-time compilation access.","path":"Settings › Debug › Environment","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":3,"row":1},{"title":"JIT Acquisition Error","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › Environment","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":3,"row":2},{"title":"Fastmem","description":"","path":"Settings › Debug › Environment","storyboard":"DebugSettings","identifier":"SearchDebug","section":3,"row":3},{"title":"Launch Times","description":"","path":"Settings › De